 \subsection{Statistical Uncertainty and Pairwise Tests}
-Table~\ref{tab:statistical_results} adds intervals for the archived scores. For the archived text pairs, 17 of 21 paired cross-model comparisons remained significant after Holm correction. The four non-significant pairs were Qwen2.5-1.5B versus Qwen2.5-3B (mean paired difference 0.0160, bootstrap 95\% CI $[0.0020,0.0303]$, rank-biserial $r=0.149$, $p_{\mathrm{Holm}}=0.1023$); Qwen2.5-3B versus Llama-3.2-3B (0.0161, 95\% CI $[0.0021,0.0305]$, $r=0.116$, $p_{\mathrm{Holm}}=0.2470$); Qwen2.5-3B versus Phi-1.5 (0.0138, 95\% CI $[-0.0012,0.0287]$, $r=0.079$, $p_{\mathrm{Holm}}=0.4765$); and Llama-3.2-3B versus Phi-1.5 ($-0.0022$, 95\% CI $[-0.0199,0.0159]$, $r=-0.009$, $p_{\mathrm{Holm}}=0.8960$). The Qwen2.5-1.5B--TinyLlama contrast was 0.5378 ($r=1.000$, $p_{\mathrm{Holm}}<0.0001$), but it includes a reference-format diagnostic and cannot establish a transfer difference. These are descriptive tests over paired prompt variants. They do not account for shared scenario templates, unverified collector inputs, reference defects, causal model effects, or decoder-seed variability.
